 React Best Practices:

Use functional components and hooks instead of class components
Implement proper React memo and useMemo for performance optimization
Follow the React hooks rules strictly
Utilize context API for state management across components
Implement error boundaries to catch and handle errors gracefully

Next.js Standards:

Utilize Next.js App Router for better performance and improved routing
Implement proper error boundaries and error handling
Use proper data fetching patterns with suspense and concurrent rendering
Leverage Next.js built-in optimizations like code splitting and image optimization
Implement server-side rendering and static site generation where appropriate

TypeScript Practices:

Use TypeScript strict mode for better type safety and catching potential errors
Follow proper type definitions and use interfaces and types effectively
Implement comprehensive error handling with proper type guards
Utilize generics for reusable components and functions
Leverage TypeScript's advanced features like conditional types and mapped types

Zod Best Practices:

Use Zod for runtime type checking and validation
Define schemas for all data structures and API responses
Implement custom validation rules where necessary
Utilize Zod's integration with React Hook Form for form validation
Leverage Zod's type inference for TypeScript integration

React Hook Form Best Practices:

Use React Hook Form for efficient form handling and validation
Implement proper form validation using Zod or Yup
Utilize the useForm hook for managing form state and validation
Leverage the Controller component for integrating with custom inputs
Implement proper error handling and display for form validation

TanStack Query Best Practices:

Use TanStack Query for efficient data fetching and caching
Implement proper query keys for cache invalidation and refetching
Utilize mutations for handling side effects and optimistic updates
Leverage the useQuery hook for fetching data and managing loading states
Implement proper error handling and retries for failed queries

Supabase Best Practices:

Use Supabase for real-time database and authentication
Implement proper error handling for database operations
Utilize Supabase's real-time capabilities for live updates
Leverage Supabase's authentication helpers for secure user management
Implement proper data validation and sanitization before database operations

Stripe Best Practices:

Use Stripe for secure payment processing
Implement proper error handling for payment operations
Utilize Stripe's client-side elements for secure card input
Leverage Stripe's server-side SDK for handling webhooks and payment intents
Implement proper PCI compliance measures for handling sensitive payment data

Axios Best Practices:

Use Axios for making HTTP requests
Implement proper error handling for network requests
Utilize Axios interceptors for adding global request/response handling
Leverage Axios' cancel token feature for cancelling ongoing requests
Implement proper timeout settings for network requests

Zustand Best Practices:

Use Zustand for simple and efficient state management
Implement proper state slicing for better performance
Utilize middleware like devtools and persist for enhanced functionality
Leverage Zustand's shallow comparison for optimized re-renders
Implement proper state normalization for complex data structures

Tailwind CSS Best Practices:

Use Tailwind CSS for utility-first styling
Implement proper responsive design using Tailwind's breakpoints
Utilize Tailwind's custom theme configuration for consistent styling
Leverage Tailwind's JIT mode for faster build times and smaller bundle sizes
Implement proper accessibility practices with Tailwind's utility classes